information and individual asymmetries can make &#x02018;personality&#x02019; an adaptation: a simple model</article-title><source>Anim. Behav</source><volume>72</volume><year>2006</year><fpage>1135</fpage><lpage>1139</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2006.04.001">doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2006.04.001</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McNamara</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Houston</surname><given-names>A.I.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Credible threats and promises</article-title><source>Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B</source><volume>357</volume><year>2002</year><fpage>1607</fpage><lpage>1616</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1098/rstb.2002.1069">doi:10.1098/rstb.2002.1069</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12495517</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McNamara</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Barta</surname><given-names>Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Houston</surname><given-names>A.I.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variation in behaviour promotes cooperation in the Prisoner's Dilemma game</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>428</volume><year>2004</year><fpage>745</fpage><lpage>748</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1038/nature02432">doi:10.1038/nature02432</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15085131</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McNamara</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Barta</surname><given-names>Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fromhage</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Houston</surname><given-names>A.I.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The coevolution of choosiness and cooperation</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>451</volume><year>2008</year><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1038/nature06455">doi:10.1038/nature06455</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18185587</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Milinski</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rockenbach</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Economics: spying on others evolves</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>317</volume><year>2007</year><fpage>464</fpage><lpage>465</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1126/science.1143918">doi:10.1126/science.1143918</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17656712</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nettle</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An evolutionary approach to the extraversion continuum</article-title><source>Evol. Hum. Behav</source><volume>26</volume><year>2005</year><fpage>363</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/j.evolhumbehav.2004.12.004">doi:10.1016/j.evolhumbehav.2004.12.004</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nettle</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The evolution of personality variation in humans and other animals</article-title><source>Am. Psychol</source><volume>61</volume><year>2006</year><fpage>622</fpage><lpage>631</lpage><ext-link ext-li